---
import '../../styles/global.css';

const title = 'Crest — From expertise to conversations';
const description = 'Crest helps experts shape an easy-to-buy entry offer and build a consistent path to relevant customer conversations.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f3f0e9" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://crestea.se/en/" />
    <link rel="alternate" hreflang="sv" href="https://crestea.se/" />
    <link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://crestea.se/en/" />
    <link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://crestea.se/" />
    <meta property="og:locale" content="en_US" />
    <meta property="og:locale:alternate" content="sv_SE" />
    <title>{title}</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="Crest, home">
        <img src="/crest-symbol-transparent.png" alt="" width="46" height="46" />
        <span>CREST</span>
      </a>
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a href="#offer">The offer</a>
        <a href="#approach">How we work</a>
        <a href="#examples">Examples</a>
      </nav>
      <div class="header-actions">
        <a class="header-cta" href="#contact">Take the first step</a>
        <div class="language-switch" aria-label="Choose language">
          <a href="/" hreflang="sv" lang="sv" aria-label="Svenska">SV</a>
          <span aria-current="page">EN</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <section class="hero" id="top">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Commercial activation for experts</p>
          <h1>From expertise<br />to <em>conversations.</em></h1>
          <p class="hero-lead">
            You are good at what you do. But when client work takes all your
            time, your next offer, next contact and next engagement are too
            easily left to chance.
          </p>
          <p class="hero-support">
            Crest turns your expertise into a sharp entry offer and creates a
            path to the people who want to know more.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button button-primary" href="#contact">Test your commercial front</a>
            <a class="text-link" href="#examples">See it in practice <span>↘</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="signal-field" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="signal-core">
            <img src="/crest-symbol-transparent.png" alt="" width="176" height="176" />
          </div>
          <span class="orbit orbit-one"></span><span class="orbit orbit-two"></span><span class="orbit orbit-three"></span>
          <span class="signal-label label-one">Expertise</span>
          <span class="signal-label label-two">Offer</span>
          <span class="signal-label label-three">Right people</span>
          <span class="signal-label label-four">Conversation</span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="recognition section-pad">
        <p class="section-number">01 / Recognition</p>
        <div class="recognition-grid">
          <h2>Fully occupied with the work you should be winning more of.</h2>
          <div class="recognition-copy">
            <p>You do not need to become better at networking. You do not need to cold-call with your cap in hand. And you certainly do not need to turn LinkedIn into a full-time job.</p>
            <p>You need a clear way for the right people to understand what you see, what you can change and how they can start working with you.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="problem-strip">
          <article><span>01</span><h3>Strong expertise</h3><p>but too broad or difficult to buy as a first step.</p></article>
          <article><span>02</span><h3>Sporadic reach</h3><p>because client work always wins the battle for your time.</p></article>
          <article><span>03</span><h3>An accidental pipeline</h3><p>built on old relationships, referrals and luck.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="commercial-front section-pad" id="offer">
        <div class="section-intro">
          <div><p class="section-number light">02 / Commercial Front</p><h2>We build the commercial front around your expertise.</h2></div>
          <p>Not an isolated campaign. Not another website left waiting. A connected path from your real expertise to a relevant conversation.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="front-path" role="list" aria-label="The four parts of a Commercial Front">
          <article role="listitem"><div class="path-marker"><span>1</span></div><h3>Position</h3><p>We find the commercially sharp edge in what you know and what you can do.</p></article>
          <article role="listitem"><div class="path-marker"><span>2</span></div><h3>Entry</h3><p>We shape a focused first engagement that delivers value and leaves people wanting more.</p></article>
          <article role="listitem"><div class="path-marker"><span>3</span></div><h3>Sales surface</h3><p>We build the place where the idea becomes clear, credible and easy to take forward.</p></article>
          <article role="listitem"><div class="path-marker"><span>4</span></div><h3>Momentum</h3><p>We find the right people, create interest and keep the dialogue moving.</p></article>
        </div>
        <div class="handover">
          <p class="handover-label">Crest takes responsibility up to this point&nbsp;</p>
          <p class="handover-copy">When someone relevant wants to know more, we hand over.<br /><strong>You take the meeting. You own the relationship. You win the business.</strong></p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="entry-offer section-pad">
        <p class="section-number">03 / An easier yes</p>
        <div class="entry-grid">
          <div>
            <h2>Your major engagement needs a smaller door.</h2>
            <p class="large-copy">Deep expertise is rarely easy to buy. So we create an entry offer: small enough to try, substantial enough to make a difference and designed to reveal how you think.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="offer-card">
            <p class="offer-kicker">A good entry offer</p>
            <ul>
              <li><span>01</span>Solves or clarifies a real problem.</li>
              <li><span>02</span>Has a clear audience, scope and output.</li>
              <li><span>03</span>Delivers standalone value — it is not a sales meeting in disguise.</li>
              <li><span>04</span>Naturally opens the door to a larger engagement.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="method section-pad" id="approach">
        <div class="section-intro dark-text">
          <div><p class="section-number">04 / How we work</p><h2>Shape. Test. Run.</h2></div>
          <p>We do not wait for the perfect plan. We make the hypothesis clear, test it with real people and improve what actually meets the market.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="method-list">
          <article><p class="method-label">Shape</p><h3>Make the expertise buyable.</h3><p>Interviews, audience, position and a defined entry offer.</p><span class="outcome">Outcome: something clear to take to market</span></article>
          <article><p class="method-label">Launch</p><h3>Let the market respond.</h3><p>Identity, campaign site, first prospect group and live outreach.</p><span class="outcome">Outcome: response, dialogue and real learning</span></article>
          <article><p class="method-label">Run</p><h3>Create consistency.</h3><p>Prospecting, contact, follow-up and continuous improvement.</p><span class="outcome">Outcome: relevant conversations without stop-start effort</span></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="proof section-pad" id="examples">
        <div class="proof-heading">
          <div><p class="section-number light">05 / In practice</p><p class="proof-brand">TWO EXAMPLES</p></div>
          <h2>The same momentum. Two very different starting points.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="case-grid">
          <article class="case-feature">
            <p class="case-type">A new commercial entry point</p><p class="case-name">EXPERTKAPITAL<span>.SE</span></p>
            <h3>A new door into a new market.</h3>
            <p>FragSheet had experience and assets, but its existing identity told the wrong story. Crest created Expertkapital: a new offer, a new surface and a new path to an entirely different audience.</p>
            <a class="text-link light-link" href="https://expertkapital.se/">Visit Expertkapital <span>↗</span></a>
          </article>
          <article class="case-feature patrik-case">
            <p class="case-type">The expert's own platform</p><p class="case-name">PATRIKHALLEN<span>.SE / .COM</span></p>
            <h3>A point of view that does not borrow someone else's brand.</h3>
            <p>Patrik needed a place to develop and collect his own perspectives as a senior adviser — with a clear boundary to his employer's brand. The result is an independent editorial identity in Swedish and English, where ideas can live longer than a post.</p>
            <div class="case-links"><a class="text-link light-link" href="https://patrikhallen.se/">Swedish <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-link light-link" href="https://patrikhallen.com/">English <span>↗</span></a></div>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="metrics-label">Expertkapital · documented campaign snapshot</p>
        <div class="metrics" aria-label="Campaign data from Expertkapital">
          <div><strong>115</strong><span>qualified prospects</span></div><div><strong>98</strong><span>initial messages</span></div><div><strong>18</strong><span>human replies</span></div><div><strong>5</strong><span>positive dialogues</span></div><div><strong>2</strong><span>meetings booked</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="metric-note">Documented campaign snapshot as of 3 September 2026. An ongoing experiment — reported without polished promises.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="fit section-pad">
        <p class="section-number">06 / Is this for you?</p>
        <div class="fit-grid">
          <div><h2>For people who want to be chosen for how they think.</h2></div>
          <div class="fit-columns">
            <article><h3>Yes, if you …</h3><ul><li>have experience that creates real client value,</li><li>can take over and sell when the right conversation begins,</li><li>want to test a clearer commercial entry point,</li><li>value relevance and integrity above volume.</li></ul></article>
            <article class="not-fit"><h3>No, if you …</h3><ul><li>want to buy a list of “warm leads”,</li><li>expect someone else to close the business,</li><li>want to send the same message to everyone,</li><li>measure success in likes rather than conversations.</li></ul></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="contact section-pad" id="contact">
        <div class="contact-mark" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/crest-symbol-transparent.png" alt="" width="120" height="120" /></div>
        <div class="contact-copy">
          <p class="section-number light">07 / The first step</p>
          <h2>What would make your expertise easier to buy?</h2>
          <p>We begin with your current position, your core offer and the audience you want to reach. Then we show you where your commercial front is strong — and where it lacks a clear way in.</p>
          <a class="button button-light" href="mailto:contact@crestea.se?subject=My commercial front">Test my commercial front</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <a class="brand footer-brand" href="#top"><img src="/crest-symbol-transparent.png" alt="" width="38" height="38" /><span>CREST</span></a>
      <p>Expertise, activated.</p><a href="mailto:contact@crestea.se">contact@crestea.se</a><p>Stockholm · Sweden</p><p>© {new Date().getFullYear()} Crest</p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
